<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><h2 class="tool-t">Appraisal readiness check</h2><i>12 questions · about two minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get written confirmation that coverage is accepted. If the claim was denied, talk to a California attorney before considering appraisal."><span>Has the insurer accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask for the full line-item estimate in writing, not just the summary page."><span>Do you have the carrier’s complete, itemized estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get an independent line-item estimate. A lump-sum bid is hard for a panel to compare."><span>Do you have your own itemized estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Gather every photo and note when each was taken. Add photos of current conditions."><span>Do you have dated photos taken soon after the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find ‘Appraisal’ in the conditions section and note the 20-day and 15-day windows."><span>Have you found the appraisal paragraph in your policy?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Suit Against Us’ clause and calendar it. Our timeline builder can help."><span>Do you know your suit-limitation date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Complete reasonable temporary repairs, such as tarping or drying, and keep every receipt."><span>Have temporary repairs been made and receipts saved?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download or request your declarations page, including any endorsements."><span>Do you have your current declarations page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure wet walls, attics, ducts and roof decking are inspected so the scope is complete."><span>Has hidden damage been opened up and documented?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Collect emails, letters and claim notes in date order."><span>Is your correspondence with the carrier organized by date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run the numbers in our appraisal payoff estimator. A small gap may not justify appraisal costs."><span>Is the gap between estimates more than about 10% or $5,000?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="List every policy that might apply, including FAIR Plan, difference-in-conditions and earthquake policies."><span>Do you know whether you have a FAIR Plan, DIC or earthquake policy too?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-reset>Reset answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out tool-out-gauge" aria-live="polite">
      <div>
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#efe3d6" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#b58150" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3" style="transition:stroke-dashoffset .5s,stroke .3s"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Your to-do list</p>
        <ul class="todo" data-o="todo"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="hint tool-note">For planning only. Results depend on what you enter and on your policy, and aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice. Nothing you type leaves your browser.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>Why readiness matters</h2>
<p>California appraisal is informal: there’s no discovery and no testimony under oath. The panel works from estimates, photos, invoices and reports. Gaps in the file usually become gaps in the award.</p>
<h2>How the score works</h2>
<p>Each question is weighted by how much it typically affects an appraisal. Coverage, estimates and photos carry the most weight. The to-do list shows only the items you answered “no.”</p>
<h2>After the check</h2>
<p>Close the gaps, then run the <a href="/claim-check-tools/appraisal-payoff-estimator/">payoff estimator</a>. If both look good, it’s a good time to talk to us.</p>

<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="qa"><details><summary>Is a high score a guarantee?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>No. It means your file has the basics a panel expects. The outcome still depends on the facts.</p></div></details><details><summary>Are my answers saved?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>No. Everything runs in your browser and resets when you leave.</p></div></details></div>
